description: Extract feature widgets from screens into widgets/ (all apps)
globs: "**/lib/features/**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Feature widgets folder

In every app, screens compose layout; reusable or non-trivial UI lives in `widgets/`—not as private classes in the screen file.

## Layout

```
lib/features/<feature>/
  widgets/
    <descriptive_name>.dart    # public StatelessWidget (or StatefulWidget)
  <feature>_screen.dart        # scaffold, app bar, wiring only
```

Example: `apps/explorer/lib/features/list/widgets/characters_list_body.dart`.

## When to extract

Move a widget out of a screen when it is:

- A named `StatelessWidget` / `StatefulWidget` that would otherwise be `_PrivateWidget`
- A distinct UI block (list body, row variant, fact row, form section)
- Shared by more than one screen **in the same feature**

Keep inline only: trivial one-off padding/`SizedBox`/`Text` with no logic.

## Naming and visibility

- File name: `snake_case.dart`; class name: `PascalCase` (no leading `_`).
- Widgets take data/callbacks via constructor params; read providers with `Consumer` / `context.read` inside the widget when needed.

## Shared UI outside a feature

| Scope | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Used by multiple features in one app | `apps/<app>/lib/widgets/` |
| Design-system / cross-app reusable UI | `sdk/thawani_ui/lib/src/widgets/` |

Do not duplicate the same widget under multiple feature folders.

## Tests

If a widget has meaningful behavior, add `test/features/<feature>/widgets/<name>_test.dart` mirroring `lib/`. Screen tests may cover simple widgets without a dedicated file.

## Do not

- Define `_ListBody`, `_Fact`, etc. at the bottom of `*_screen.dart`
- Put providers or use cases in widget files—only consume them
- Put feature-specific UI in app-root `lib/widgets/` (use `features/<feature>/widgets/`)
